**Constraints:** The property is in the Burnside Conservation Area. It is not listed, and there is no tree preservation order.

**Council guidance on outbuildings:** A garden room or shed usually does not need an application if it meets all of these conditions:
- It is under 2.5 metres high.
- It sits behind the front wall of the house.
- It covers less than half of the garden.

**What this means for you:** Because the property is in a conservation area, the general [withheld] development allowance is more restricted than the guidance above suggests. Outbuildings there may need an application even when they meet those size limits, particularly if the building would be visible from the lane. I can't give a formal opinion on whether your proposal needs permission. Only the planning team can confirm that.

